                <pb facs="0418" n="308" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg308"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.6363/2550: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morrow</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-04-16T18:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 16,
                                1928—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 9:45 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>112. Department’s telegram 101 for the [Ambassador]. We are advised by Branch
                    that newspaper report as set out by you is correct. Branch was received by
                    President Calles at 1 o’clock Saturday, April 14, and informed the President of
                    the Huasteca Company’s intention to make application at once for confirmatory
                    concessions under the amended petroleum law and regulations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morrow</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
